{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not take interest from your brother.</b> Above it spoke of the poor man and the sojourner, and here of your brother — even a rich man. It is juxtaposed here because it mentioned the foreign servant, to tell you that even though it is written of him 'you shall not oppress him,' you have permission to take from him the fee for the loan."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:00.289456281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}